comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-27T11:05:09.295Z",codex-agent,"Claimed. Plan: (1) reproduce the three polynomial-ReDoS paths with a timing harness, (2) replace the backtracking ATX heading regex with a single-pass linear parser shared by paragraph() and sectionPath(), (3) make the JSON span tokenizer provably linear (regex-free scanning), (4) table-driven equivalence tests against the old regex plus adversarial timing tests that fail on revert, (5) rebuild dist, run targeted gates, PR."
  "2026-11-27T11:30:39.164Z",codex-agent,"Reproduction confirmed on the retired heading regex: 800-char hostile space run => 1.7s, 1600 => 13.1s (~n^2.8 growth); a 50,000-char line extrapolates to hours, so cited-document verification stalls. The retired JSON tokenizer measured LINEAR on every adversarial probe (1MB escaped string 0.03ms, 500k escape pairs 0.2ms, 1MB digits 0.1ms, 1MB whitespace 220ms via a per-char regex test) - alert #1 is analyzed as a CodeQL false positive on an unambiguous alternation, but the tokenizer is rewritten regex-free anyway so the alert closes mechanically and linearity is provable by construction. Design: (1) new single-pass per-line ATX parser (headingLines) shared by paragraph() and sectionPath(), byte-identical to the retired regex (proven by curated corpus + 400 seeded random documents); it reproduces the exact lazy-title and CR-swallow span semantics; (2) json-spans.ts scanner has no regex at all: code-unit string/number/literal scanning, JSON.parse still decodes object keys; (3) new tests: heading-parity.test.ts (corpus + differential + 50k budget + retired-regex child probe killed at 400ms), json-spans-linear.test.ts (string-token differential vs the retired sticky regex + hostile budgets incl. the 8MB whitespace that fails on revert); (4) two function-scope revert cases added to the repo's revert harness, both yielding negativeControl fail 1."
  "2026-11-27T11:34:55.519Z",codex-agent,"Gates so far: typecheck clean, lint clean, docstring gate clean (27 files, 131 declarations), duplication 0%, identity:check 0 violations. pm health --strict-exit fails ONLY on the pre-existing local-environment warning extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew (a home-installed pm-github extension copy carries a newer pm-cli than the repo pin; tracked by the open local-extension-skew chore item; the repo tree is untouched by this work and fresh CI clones do not see it). Function-scope revert proofs run through the repo harness: linear heading scan and linear JSON whitespace both yield negativeControl fail 1 with sources restored byte-identically."
